    "goal": "Report PLINK binary dataset sizes for a GWAS cohort of 134 samples and 7,501,270 variants (largest chromosome 793,937 variants).",
    "rationale": "PLINK binary .bed packs 2 bits per sample per variant (4 samples per byte). Total .bed size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB; per-chromosome .bed size uses the same rule on the largest chromosome's variant count. The number of per-chromosome files is assumed to be the standard human GWAS split of 25 chromosomes (22 autosomes + X + Y + MT), which is consistent with the largest chromosome carrying ~794k of the ~7.5M total variants.",
